    <item>
      <title>Extracting Nested JSON Content from Python Dictionary Structure</title>
      <link>https://sqlpey.com/python/nested-json-extraction-techniques/</link>
      <pubDate>Tue, 04 Nov 2025 00:00:00 +0000</pubDate>
      <guid>https://sqlpey.com/python/nested-json-extraction-techniques/</guid>
      <description>&lt;h2 id=&#34;extracting-nested-json-content-from-python-dictionary-structure&#34;&gt;&amp;ldquo;Extracting Nested JSON Content from Python Dictionary Structure&amp;rdquo;&lt;/h2&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;When dealing with data structures returned from APIs or processes, it is common to encounter situations where a dictionary key holds a string that must be parsed again as JSON. Consider the following sample data structure, which illustrates this nested string issue:&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;div class=&#34;highlight&#34;&gt;&lt;pre tabindex=&#34;0&#34; style=&#34;color:#f8f8f2;background-color:#272822;-moz-tab-size:4;-o-tab-size:4;tab-size:4;&#34;&gt;&lt;code class=&#34;language-python&#34; data-lang=&#34;python&#34;&gt;&lt;span style=&#34;display:flex;&#34;&gt;&lt;span&gt;data_sample &lt;span style=&#34;color:#f92672&#34;&gt;=&lt;/span&gt; {&#xA;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&#34;display:flex;&#34;&gt;&lt;span&gt;    &lt;span style=&#34;color:#e6db74&#34;&gt;&amp;#39;data&amp;#39;&lt;/span&gt;: {&#xA;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&#34;display:flex;&#34;&gt;&lt;span&gt;        &lt;span style=&#34;color:#e6db74&#34;&gt;&amp;#39;time&amp;#39;&lt;/span&gt;: &lt;span style=&#34;color:#e6db74&#34;&gt;&amp;#39;1515580011&amp;#39;&lt;/span&gt;,&#xA;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&#34;display:flex;&#34;&gt;&lt;span&gt;        &lt;span style=&#34;color:#e6db74&#34;&gt;&amp;#39;video_info&amp;#39;&lt;/span&gt;: [{&#xA;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&#34;display:flex;&#34;&gt;&lt;span&gt;            &lt;span style=&#34;color:#e6db74&#34;&gt;&amp;#39;announcement&amp;#39;&lt;/span&gt;: (&#xA;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&#34;display:flex;&#34;&gt;&lt;span&gt;            &lt;span style=&#34;color:#e6db74&#34;&gt;&amp;#34;&amp;#34;&amp;#34;{&#xA;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&#34;display:flex;&#34;&gt;&lt;span&gt;&lt;span style=&#34;color:#e6db74&#34;&gt;                &amp;#34;announcement_id&amp;#34;: &amp;#34;6&amp;#34;,&#xA;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&#34;display:flex;&#34;&gt;&lt;span&gt;&lt;span style=&#34;color:#e6db74&#34;&gt;                &amp;#34;name&amp;#34;: &amp;#34;INS&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&#34;color:#ae81ff&#34;&gt;\\&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&#34;color:#e6db74&#34;&gt;u8d26&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&#34;color:#ae81ff&#34;&gt;\\&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&#34;color:#e6db74&#34;&gt;u53f7&amp;#34;,&#xA;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&#34;display:flex;&#34;&gt;&lt;span&gt;&lt;span style=&#34;color:#e6db74&#34;&gt;                &amp;#34;icon&amp;#34;: &amp;#34;http:&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&#34;color:#ae81ff&#34;&gt;\\\\&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&#34;color:#e6db74&#34;&gt;/&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&#34;color:#ae81ff&#34;&gt;\\\\&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&#34;color:#e6db74&#34;&gt;/liveme.cms.ksmobile.net&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&#34;color:#ae81ff&#34;&gt;\\\\&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&#34;color:#e6db74&#34;&gt;/live&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&#34;color:#ae81ff&#34;&gt;\\\\&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&#34;color:#e6db74&#34;&gt;/announcement&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&#34;color:#ae81ff&#34;&gt;\\\\&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&#34;color:#e6db74&#34;&gt;/2017-08-18_19:44:54&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&#34;color:#ae81ff&#34;&gt;\\\\&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&#34;color:#e6db74&#34;&gt;/ins.png&amp;#34;,&#xA;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&#34;display:flex;&#34;&gt;&lt;span&gt;&lt;span style=&#34;color:#e6db74&#34;&gt;                &amp;#34;icon_new&amp;#34;: &amp;#34;http:&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&#34;color:#ae81ff&#34;&gt;\\\\&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&#34;color:#e6db74&#34;&gt;/&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&#34;color:#ae81ff&#34;&gt;\\\\&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&#34;color:#e6db74&#34;&gt;/liveme.cms.ksmobile.net&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&#34;color:#ae81ff&#34;&gt;\\\\&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&#34;color:#e6db74&#34;&gt;/live&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&#34;color:#ae81ff&#34;&gt;\\\\&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&#34;color:#e6db74&#34;&gt;/announcement&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&#34;color:#ae81ff&#34;&gt;\\\\&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&#34;color:#e6db74&#34;&gt;/2017-10-20_22:24:38&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&#34;color:#ae81ff&#34;&gt;\\\\&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&#34;color:#e6db74&#34;&gt;/4.png&amp;#34;,&#xA;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&#34;display:flex;&#34;&gt;&lt;span&gt;&lt;span style=&#34;color:#e6db74&#34;&gt;                &amp;#34;videoid&amp;#34;: &amp;#34;15154610218328614178&amp;#34;,&#xA;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&#34;display:flex;&#34;&gt;&lt;span&gt;&lt;span style=&#34;color:#e6db74&#34;&gt;                &amp;#34;content&amp;#34;: &amp;#34;FOLLOW ME PLEASE&amp;#34;,&#xA;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&#34;display:flex;&#34;&gt;&lt;span&gt;&lt;span style=&#34;color:#e6db74&#34;&gt;                &amp;#34;x_coordinate&amp;#34;: &amp;#34;0.22&amp;#34;,&#xA;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&#34;display:flex;&#34;&gt;&lt;span&gt;&lt;span style=&#34;color:#e6db74&#34;&gt;                &amp;#34;y_coordinate&amp;#34;: &amp;#34;0.23&amp;#34;&#xA;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&#34;display:flex;&#34;&gt;&lt;span&gt;&lt;span style=&#34;color:#e6db74&#34;&gt;            }&amp;#34;&amp;#34;&amp;#34;&lt;/span&gt;),&#xA;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&#34;display:flex;&#34;&gt;&lt;span&gt;            &lt;span style=&#34;color:#e6db74&#34;&gt;&amp;#39;announcement_shop&amp;#39;&lt;/span&gt;: &lt;span style=&#34;color:#e6db74&#34;&gt;&amp;#39;&amp;#39;&lt;/span&gt;&#xA;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&#34;display:flex;&#34;&gt;&lt;span&gt;        }]&#xA;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&#34;display:flex;&#34;&gt;&lt;span&gt;    },&#xA;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&#34;display:flex;&#34;&gt;&lt;span&gt;    &lt;span style=&#34;color:#e6db74&#34;&gt;&amp;#39;msg&amp;#39;&lt;/span&gt;: &lt;span style=&#34;color:#e6db74&#34;&gt;&amp;#39;&amp;#39;&lt;/span&gt;,&#xA;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&#34;display:flex;&#34;&gt;&lt;span&gt;    &lt;span style=&#34;color:#e6db74&#34;&gt;&amp;#39;status&amp;#39;&lt;/span&gt;: &lt;span style=&#34;color:#e6db74&#34;&gt;&amp;#39;200&amp;#39;&lt;/span&gt;&#xA;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&#34;display:flex;&#34;&gt;&lt;span&gt;}&#xA;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;p&gt;The target value, &lt;code&gt;&amp;quot;FOLLOW ME PLEASE&amp;quot;&lt;/code&gt;, is nested within the &lt;code&gt;&#39;content&#39;&lt;/code&gt; key, which is inside a JSON string located at &lt;code&gt;data[&#39;data&#39;][&#39;video_info&#39;][0][&#39;announcement&#39;]&lt;/code&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;</description>
    </item>
    <item>
      <title>Resolve `IllegalStateException: Expected BEGIN_OBJECT but was STRING` in JSON Parsing</title>
      <link>https://sqlpey.com/java/illegalstateexception-expected-begin-object-but-was-string/</link>
      <pubDate>Tue, 04 Nov 2025 00:00:00 +0000</pubDate>
      <guid>https://sqlpey.com/java/illegalstateexception-expected-begin-object-but-was-string/</guid>
      <description>&lt;h2 id=&#34;resolve-illegalstateexception-expected-begin_object-but-was-string-in-json-parsing&#34;&gt;&amp;ldquo;Resolve &lt;code&gt;IllegalStateException: Expected BEGIN_OBJECT but was STRING&lt;/code&gt; in JSON Parsing&amp;rdquo;&lt;/h2&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;This prevalent error, &lt;code&gt;java.lang.IllegalStateException: Expected BEGIN_OBJECT but was STRING at line X column Y&lt;/code&gt;, typically arises when a JSON parsing library, such as Gson, anticipates a JSON object (starting with &lt;code&gt;{&lt;/code&gt;) but encounters a JSON string (starting with &lt;code&gt;&amp;quot;&lt;/code&gt;) instead. This mismatch in expected structure is a common pitfall when processing data from APIs or local files. Let&amp;rsquo;s delve into various scenarios and effective remedies.&lt;/p&gt;</description>
    </item>
    <item>
      <title>Solved-How-to-Parse-JSON-in-Java-with-Leading-Libraries</title>
      <link>https://sqlpey.com/java/solved-how-to-parse-json-in-java-with-leading-libraries/</link>
      <pubDate>Wed, 23 Jul 2025 00:00:00 +0000</pubDate>
      <guid>https://sqlpey.com/java/solved-how-to-parse-json-in-java-with-leading-libraries/</guid>
      <description>&lt;h2 id=&#34;solved-how-to-parse-json-in-java-with-leading-libraries&#34;&gt;&amp;ldquo;Solved-How-to-Parse-JSON-in-Java-with-Leading-Libraries&amp;rdquo;&lt;/h2&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;Parsing JSON data is a fundamental task for many Java applications, especially when dealing with web services and APIs. JSON (JavaScript Object Notation) has become the de-facto standard for data interchange due to its lightweight nature and human-readable format. This guide delves into various effective methods and popular libraries available in Java to parse JSON strings, extract values, and map them to Java objects.&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;Let&amp;rsquo;s consider a common JSON structure we&amp;rsquo;ll use as an example throughout this guide:&lt;/p&gt;</description>
    </item>
